   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\frac{(-1 + t)^{4} - 1}{t} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(-1 + t) - f(-1) \\) with \\( f(x) = x^{4} \\), because \\( f(-1) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = x^{4} \\) and the base point is \\( x = -1 \\).",
         "mathjson": -1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(-1) \\), and \\( f'(x) = 4 x^{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            4,
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(-1) = -4 \\).",
         "mathjson": -4
      }
   ],
